------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Opcode 35 (octal) in the address class is listed as 'available' in the INDJUMP table. The entry at that position is 'TCF' with no target (Comanche055 line 334). If reached, this would execute whatever instruction follows the incomplete TCF. Whether yaYUL assembles this as a no-op, a trap, or an undefined jump is unclear from the source alone. Can interpretive programs ever generate this opcode?"

open question "What happens if PUSHLOC underflows below FIXLOC? The interpreter decrements PUSHLOC by 2, 3 or 6 words depending on MODE, but there is no bounds check. If interpretive code pushes more data than the VAC area can hold, PUSHLOC will point below the VAC area base and subsequent stores will corrupt adjacent memory. Is this a known constraint that callers must respect, or is it a latent bug?"

open question "INTBIT15 prevents cross-superbank references from interpretive code. Are there any known cases where interpretive programs need to reference data or code across the superbank boundary? If so, how is this handled — does the program EXIT to basic code, perform the cross-bank operation, then re-enter the interpreter?"
